{"title": "Reasoning Super Practice — Mock #26", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '1'.</p><p><img width=304 height=131 id=\"Picture 12\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22005/image027.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; '1' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"304\" height=\"131\" id=\"Picture 12\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22005/image027.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["2", "6", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["2", "6", "3", "4"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>From figure 1 and figure 3 we can see that number adjacent to '4' and '6' are '1' and '2'.</p><p>Which means the numbers '1' and '2' will be on the opposite side of the dice.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From figure 1 and figure 3 we can see that number adjacent to '4' and '6' are '1' and '2'.</p><p>Which means the numbers '1' and '2' will be on the opposite side of the dice.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '2'.</p><p><img width=506 height=224 id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24204/image007.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; '2' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"506\" height=\"224\" id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24204/image007.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["4", "3", "6", "5"], "options_hi": ["4", "3", "6", "5"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>From the 1<sup>st</sup> and 2<sup>nd</sup> figure, opposite faces are 1 and 6.</p><p>From the 2<sup>nd</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> figure, opposite faces are 3 and 4.</p><p>Which means the face opposite to the face showing 2 will be 5. </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From the 1<sup>st</sup> and 2<sup>nd</sup> figure, opposite faces are 1 and 6.</p><p>From the 2<sup>nd</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> figure, opposite faces are 3 and 4.</p><p>Which means the face opposite to the face showing 2 will be 5. </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the symbol that will be on the face opposite to the face having 'N '.</p><p><img width=343 height=104 id=\"Picture 54\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19586/image012.png\" alt=1.png></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2330;&#2367;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379; 'N' &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"343\" height=\"104\" id=\"Picture 54\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19586/image012.png\" alt=\"1.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["#", "&amp;", "%", "@"], "options_hi": ["#", "&amp;", "%", "@"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=115 height=113 id=\"Picture 55\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19586/image013.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>The symbol that will be on the face opposite to the face having 'N ' will be '#'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=115 height=113 id=\"Picture 55\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19586/image013.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>The symbol that will be on the face opposite to the face having 'N ' will be '#'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '3'.</p><p><img width=355 height=154 id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24442/image029.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; '3' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"355\" height=\"154\" id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24442/image029.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["4", "1", "5", "2"], "options_hi": ["4", "1", "5", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The numbers adjacent to number '5' are '3', '4', '1', and '2'. Also, numbers '3' and '4' are adjacent to each other which means either '1' or '2' will be opposite to number '3'. </p><p>From the figure 3 we can observe that the number '1' and '4' are adjacent to each other. Which means numbers '3' and '1' must be opposite to each other.</p><p>Hence, the number on the face opposite the face showing '3' will be '1'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The numbers adjacent to number '5' are '3', '4', '1', and '2'. Also, numbers '3' and '4' are adjacent to each other which means either '1' or '2' will be opposite to number '3'. </p><p>From the figure 3 we can observe that the number '1' and '4' are adjacent to each other. Which means numbers '3' and '1' must be opposite to each other.</p><p>Hence, the number on the face opposite the face showing '3' will be '1'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '1'.</p><p><img width=386 height=172 id=\"Picture 20\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23217/image021.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; '1' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"386\" height=\"172\" id=\"Picture 20\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23217/image021.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["6", "2", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["6", "2", "3", "4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>In all the 3 figures, we can see '1' at the top and number '3' is not visible. Only the face opposite to face bearing number '1' will not be visible.</p><p>Hence, the face opposite to face showing '1' will be '3'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In all the 3 figures, we can see '1' at the top and number '3' is not visible. Only the face opposite to face bearing number '1' will not be visible.</p><p>Hence, the face opposite to face showing '1' will be '3'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the symbol that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '@'.</p><p><img width=415 height=144 id=\"Picture 58\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19259/image031.png\" alt=1.png></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; '@' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"415\" height=\"144\" id=\"Picture 58\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19259/image031.png\" alt=\"1.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["!", "&lt;", "&amp;", "#"], "options_hi": ["!", "&lt;", "&amp;", "#"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=169 height=162 id=\"Picture 60\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19259/image032.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>The symbol that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '@' is '#'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=169 height=162 id=\"Picture 60\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19259/image032.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>The symbol that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '@' is '#'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Six letters M, N, O, P, Q and R are written on different faces of a dice. Two positions of this dice are shown in the figure. Find the letter on the face opposite to a vowel.</p><p><img width=187 height=93 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24212/image001.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2331;&#2361; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; - M, N, O, P, Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2310;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"187\" height=\"93\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24212/image001.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["M", "N", "P", "R"], "options_hi": ["M", "N", "P", "R"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>After opening both the dices: </p><p><img width=78 height=74 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24212/image002.png\"></p><p>And, </p><p><img width=76 height=72 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24212/image003.png\"></p><p>After merging both the images: </p><p><img width=112 height=139 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24212/image004.png\"></p><p>Hence, the face opposite to O will be R. </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>After opening both the dices: </p><p><img width=78 height=74 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24212/image002.png\"></p><p>And, </p><p><img width=76 height=72 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24212/image003.png\"></p><p>After merging both the images: </p><p><img width=112 height=139 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24212/image004.png\"></p><p>Hence, the face opposite to O will be R. </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A cube is made by folding the given sheet. In the cube so formed, which of the following pairs of numbers would be opposite to each other?</p><p><img width=157 height=119 id=\"Picture 35\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image009.jpg\" ></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p><img width=\"157\" height=\"119\" id=\"Picture 35\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image009.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["1 and 6", "4 and 5", "3 and 4", "6 and 3"], "options_hi": ["1 &#2324;&#2352; 6", "4 &#2324;&#2352; 5", "3 &#2324;&#2352; 4", "6 &#2324;&#2352; 3"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Here, faces 1 and 2, 6 and 5, <b>3 and 4</b> would be opposite to each other.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, faces 1 and 2, 6 and 5, <b>3 and 4</b> would be opposite to each other.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A cube is made by folding the given sheet. In the cube so formed, what would be the letter on the face opposite the face showing the letter 'A'?</p><p><img width=154 height=170 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19517/image029.png\" alt=1.png></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; 'A' &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p><img width=\"154\" height=\"170\" id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19517/image029.png\" alt=\"1.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["V", "I", "E", "U"], "options_hi": ["V", "I", "E", "U"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=164 height=149 id=\"Picture 10\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19517/image030.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>So, I is the letter on the face opposite the face showing the letter 'A'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=164 height=149 id=\"Picture 10\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19517/image030.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>So, I is the letter on the face opposite the face showing the letter 'A'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A cube is made by folding the given sheet. In the cube so formed, which of the following pairs of numbers will be on opposite sides?</p><p><img width=151 height=222 id=\"Picture 54\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19374/image019.png\" alt=1.png></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p><img width=\"151\" height=\"222\" id=\"Picture 54\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19374/image019.png\" alt=\"1.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["1 and 2", "2 and 4", "1 and 5", "3 and 6"], "options_hi": ["1 &#2324;&#2352; 2", "2 &#2324;&#2352; 4", "1 &#2324;&#2352; 5", "3 &#2324;&#2352; 6"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=201 height=180 id=\"Picture 55\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19374/image020.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>So, 2 is opposite to 4 in the cube formed.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=201 height=180 id=\"Picture 55\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19374/image020.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>So, 2 is opposite to 4 in the cube formed.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Two different positions of the same dice are shown, the faces of which are marked with the letters - F, G, H, I, J and K. Select the letter that will be on the face opposite to the face having the letter 'F '.</p><p><img width=234 height=83 id=\"Picture 43\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19589/image018.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; - F, G, H, I, J &#2324;&#2352; K &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; 'F' &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"234\" height=\"83\" id=\"Picture 43\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19589/image018.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["J", "G", "H", "I"], "options_hi": ["J", "G", "H", "I"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Every face is adjacent to four other faces in a cube. In the given combinations, J is adjacent to F, I, H, and G. Hence, K is opposite of J.</p><p>Also, if we change the orientation of the first cube, we get,</p><p><img width=234 height=83 id=\"Picture 44\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19589/image019.jpg\" ></p><p>Here, we can say that the faces J and K, <b>F and G</b>, and I and H are opposite to each other.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Every face is adjacent to four other faces in a cube. In the given combinations, J is adjacent to F, I, H, and G. Hence, K is opposite of J.</p><p>Also, if we change the orientation of the first cube, we get,</p><p><img width=234 height=83 id=\"Picture 44\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19589/image019.jpg\" ></p><p>Here, we can say that the faces J and K, <b>F and G</b>, and I and H are opposite to each other.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '1'.</p><p><img width=404 height=171 id=\"Picture 33\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24446/image037.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; '1' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"404\" height=\"171\" id=\"Picture 33\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24446/image037.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["3", "4", "6", "2"], "options_hi": ["3", "4", "6", "2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>From figures 1 and 2, the faces adjacent to the face 1 are 3, 4, 5, and 6. Which means the face opposite to the face showing '1' will be '2'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From figures 1 and 2, the faces adjacent to the face 1 are 3, 4, 5, and 6. Which means the face opposite to the face showing '1' will be '2'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '1'.</p><p><img width=324 height=150 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24508/image005.png\" ></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; '1' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2380;&#2332;&#2370;&#2342; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"324\" height=\"150\" id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24508/image005.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["5", "6", "2", "3"], "options_hi": ["5", "6", "2", "3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>From the 2<sup>nd</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> dice, we can observe that faces adjacent to faces (6 and 2) are 1 and 3. Which means the faces 1 and 3 will be opposite to each other.</p><p>Hence, the face opposite to face 3 will be 1.</p><p>So, option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From the 2<sup>nd</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> dice, we can observe that faces adjacent to faces (6 and 2) are 1 and 3. Which means the faces 1 and 3 will be opposite to each other.</p><p>Hence, the face opposite to face 3 will be 1.</p><p>So, option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '1'.</p><p><img width=340 height=144 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24566/image010.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; '1' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"340\" height=\"144\" id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24566/image010.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["5", "6", "2", "3"], "options_hi": ["5", "6", "2", "3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>From figures 1 and 2 we can see that the numbers adjacent to the face showing number '1' are '4', '5', '6', and '2'.</p><p>Which means the face opposite to the face showing '1' will be '3'.</p><p>Hence, option (d) is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From figures 1 and 2 we can see that the numbers adjacent to the face showing number '1' are '4', '5', '6', and '2'.</p><p>Which means the face opposite to the face showing '1' will be '3'.</p><p>Hence, option (d) is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '4'.</p><p><img width=363 height=155 id=\"Picture 27\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23217/image032.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; '4' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"363\" height=\"155\" id=\"Picture 27\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23217/image032.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["5", "6", "2", "3"], "options_hi": ["5", "6", "2", "3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>From figure 1 and 3, we can see that the faces adjacent to the faces 5 and 6 are 3 and 4. Which means the faces 3 and 4 will be opposite to each other.</p><p>Hence, option (d) is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From figure 1 and 3, we can see that the faces adjacent to the faces 5 and 6 are 3 and 4. Which means the faces 3 and 4 will be opposite to each other.</p><p>Hence, option (d) is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A cube is made by folding the given sheet. In the cube so formed, which of the following pairs of letters will be on opposite sides?</p><p><img width=275 height=107 id=\"Picture 33\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19398/image001.png\" alt=1.png></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p><img width=\"275\" height=\"107\" id=\"Picture 33\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19398/image001.png\" alt=\"1.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["Q and E", "L and U", "B and E", "A and Q"], "options_hi": ["Q &#2324;&#2352; E", "L &#2324;&#2352; U", "B &#2324;&#2352; E", "A &#2324;&#2352; Q"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=172 height=169 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19398/image002.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>So, in the cube so formed, Q and E will be on opposite sides.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=172 height=169 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19398/image002.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>So, in the cube so formed, Q and E will be on opposite sides.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three different positions of the same dice are shown. Find the number on the face opposite the face showing '2'.</p><p><img width=318 height=127 id=\"Picture 46\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22052/image022.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; '2' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"318\" height=\"127\" id=\"Picture 46\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22052/image022.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["6", "3", "4", "1"], "options_hi": ["6", "3", "4", "1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>From the figure 2 and 3, we can see that the numbers adjacent to the numbers 3 and 5 are '2' and '4'. Which means the numbers '2' and '4' will be on the opposite side of the dice.</p><p>So, the number opposite to '2' in the dice will be '4'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From the figure 2 and 3, we can see that the numbers adjacent to the numbers 3 and 5 are '2' and '4'. Which means the numbers '2' and '4' will be on the opposite side of the dice.</p><p>So, the number opposite to '2' in the dice will be '4'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the symbol that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '&lt;'.</p><p><img width=468 height=149 id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19217/image021.png\" alt=1.png></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; '&lt;' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"468\" height=\"149\" id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19217/image021.png\" alt=\"1.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["@", "$", "&amp;", "#"], "options_hi": ["@", "$", "&amp;", "#"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Since, face showing % is adjacent to the faces showing $, @, &amp; and &lt;, so face showing # will be opposite to the one showing %.</p><p>Now, from the orientations of the figures, it's clear that face showing $ is opposite to the one showing &amp; and the face showing &lt; is opposite to the one showing @.</p><p>So, the symbol that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '&lt;' will be '@'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since, face showing % is adjacent to the faces showing $, @, &amp; and &lt;, so face showing # will be opposite to the one showing %.</p><p>Now, from the orientations of the figures, it's clear that face showing $ is opposite to the one showing &amp; and the face showing &lt; is opposite to the one showing @.</p><p>So, the symbol that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '&lt;' will be '@'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Four different positions of the same dice are shown, the six faces of which are numbered 1 to 6. Select the number that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '4'.</p><p><img width=361 height=122 id=\"Picture 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21957/image019.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2361; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; 1 &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2332;&#2379; '4' &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"361\" height=\"122\" id=\"Picture 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21957/image019.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "3", "5"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "3", "5"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>From 1<sup>st</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> dice, we can see that numbers '1' and '4' are adjacent to numbers '6' and '3'. Which means, '1' and '4' will be opposite to each other.</p><p>Hence, number which will be opposite to '4' on the dice will be '1'.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From 1<sup>st</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> dice, we can see that numbers '1' and '4' are adjacent to numbers '6' and '3'. Which means, '1' and '4' will be opposite to each other.</p><p>Hence, number which will be opposite to '4' on the dice will be '1'.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Select the dice that can be formed by folding the given sheet along the lines.</p><p><img width=592 height=437 id=\"Picture 27\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19316/image006.png\" alt=1.png></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2342;&#2367;&#2358; &#2350;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"592\" height=\"437\" id=\"Picture 27\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19316/image006.png\" alt=\"1.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["Only A and B", "Only A", "Only B", "Only C and D"], "options_hi": ["&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; A &#2324;&#2352; B", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; A", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; B", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; C &#2324;&#2352; D"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=169 height=159 id=\"Picture 44\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19316/image007.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>The dice that can be formed by folding the given sheet along the lines is the only dice in option figure (A).</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=169 height=159 id=\"Picture 44\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19316/image007.png\" alt=1.png></p><p>The dice that can be formed by folding the given sheet along the lines is the only dice in option figure (A).</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}]}